      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we have 4 positions on the team, and Jordan is fixed to run in the fourth position. So we need to calculate permutations of the remaining 3 spots among the 3 remaining runners. The number of permutations of the remaining runners can be calculated using Python:\n\n1. We import the `math` module which contains the permutation function `math.perm`.\n2. We define a range for the runners, which goes from 1 to `n - 1` for `n` total runners, since Jordan is always fixed in the fourth position.\n3. The permutation of these `n - 1` runners is calculated using `math.perm(3, n - 1)`.\n\nLet's calculate the result using Python:\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Jordan is fixed in the fourth position, so there are 3 positions left to arrange the other runners.\ntotal_runners = 4\n# The number of runners excluding Jordan is 3.\nmortals = range(1, total_runners)\n# Calculate the number of permutations of these 3 mortals.\nperm = math.perm(3, total_runners - 3)\nformat(perm)\n```\n```output\nDone\n```\nThe final answer, which represents the number of different orders the four team members can run, assuming that Jordan runs the fourth lap, is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
